## 9. Trie

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = {};
    this.isEnd = false;
  }
}

class Trie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }

  insert(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const c of word) {
      if (!node.children[c]) node.children[c] = new TrieNode();
      node = node.children[c];
    }
    node.isEnd = true;
  }

  search(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const c of word) {
      if (!node.children[c]) return false;
      node = node.children[c];
    }
    return node.isEnd;
  }
}
```

**Use cases:** Autocomplete, word search, prefix matching.

